From ec4e4f78285892b7eaea312c1c547722e13824c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jean Humann <jeanhumann@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 5 Jul 2026 03:03:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: implement distributed_sequence_id for pandas API on
 Spark

Implement the internal Spark function distributed_sequence_id(), which
pyspark.pandas uses over Spark Connect to attach its default
distributed-sequence index. Previously any pandas-on-Spark operation
that attached a default index to a server-side frame (ps.range(),
DataFrame.pandas_api(), merge(), read_parquet(), ...) failed with
"unknown function: distributed_sequence_id".

The implementation follows the existing monotonically_increasing_id
pattern:

- a marker scalar UDF registered as distributed_sequence_id
- a plan rewriter that replaces the marker with a column emitted by a
  new DistributedSequenceIdNode logical extension node
- a DistributedSequenceIdExec physical operator that attaches a
  gap-free, 0-based Int64 sequence in input order by draining input
  partitions sequentially into a single output partition
- proto codec support so the operator works in distributed execution

With this change, pyspark.pandas works against Sail with the default
index type, without requiring compute.default_index_type to be set to
"distributed".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
